@startuml

title The scheduled start: the message one firing publishes

class "scheduled start\n(workflow.v1.start)" as scheduled_start <<message>> #E1F5FF {
    {field} +workflow type : name
    {field} +tenant : tenant id
    {field} +request payload : text
    {field} +correlation identifier : text
    {field} +instance identifier : text
}

note top of scheduled_start
Opens the run a firing carries: the job names the run and the run takes the work.
name workflow type // the definition the run follows
tenant id tenant // the tenant the run acts for
text request payload // the material every step builder reads
text correlation identifier // ties the run to the originating request
text instance identifier // the firing's own identity, so a repeated publish of one firing is the same run
end note

@enduml
